rt\": 37902, \"value\": 288}], \"metric\": \"event_count\", \"window\": [4302, 42701]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 51311, "tokens_after": 51311, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2025d7ec", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [798, 131, 389, 972, 1877, 1932], "window": [4302, 42701], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "798 and 131 are 2 hops apart in the static graph only through the high-degree hub 389, but the hub edge incident to 131 is directed 131->389, so no directed route to 131 exists. Temporal reachability from 798 under the 600-unit constraint reaches just 3 nodes and misses 131; crucially, dropping the max_wait constraint entirely still fails to reach 131 despite covering 650 nodes, showing the failure is one of direction/ordering rather than delay. None of 131's three in-neighbours (972, 1877, 1932) is temporally reachable from 798. Both nodes are active and the window is densely populated, so sparsity and inactivity are ruled out; the apparent link is an artefact of hub popularity and time-agnostic connectivity. No genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Findings\n\n**Static connectivity exists but is a red herring.** 798 sits 2 hops from 131 via the hub node 389 (step_05): 798\u2192389 (step_06) and 131\u2192389 (step_15). But that second edge points *away* from 131 (389 never contacts 131), so the \"connection when time is ignored\" is not even a usable directed route.\n\n**No time-respecting path, with or without the delay constraint.**\n- With max_wait = 600: unreachable, and 798's forward temporal cone contains only 3 nodes total (step_02).\n- Relaxing the constraint entirely (no max_wait): 798 reaches 650 nodes, and 131 is *still* not among them (step_04). So the failure is not caused by the 600-unit gap rule \u2014 it is a directional/ordering failure.\n- Path enumeration returns zero routes (step_13); reverse direction also fails (step_16).\n\n**Confounder controls.**\n- Volume: the window holds 4954 events across 1888 nodes with steady activity in every bin (step_01, step_17), so there is no data sparsity or dead interval to blame.\n- Popularity: 389 is a very high-degree hub (151 partners, step_14), which is exactly why ignoring time makes 798 and 131 look linked; 131's only in-contacts are 972, 1877, 1932 (step_08), none of which is temporally reachable from 798 (step_11, step_12).\n- Both endpoints are active within the window (798: 4 events, 131: 7 events \u2014 step_03), spread across bins (step_09, step_10), so absence is not from inactivity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2025d7ec\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131, 389, 972, 1877, 1932],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"798 and 131 are 2 hops apart in the static graph only through the high-degree hub 389, but the hub edge incident to 131 is directed 131->389, so no directed route to 131 exists. Temporal reachability from 798 under the 600-unit constraint reaches just 3 nodes and misses 131; crucially, dropping the max_wait constraint entirely still fails to reach 131 despite covering 650 nodes, showing the failure is one of direction/ordering rather than delay. None of 131's three in-neighbours (972, 1877, 1932) is temporally reachable from 798. Both nodes are active and the window is densely populated, so sparsity and inactivity are ruled out; the apparent link is an artefact of hub popularity and time-agnostic connectivity. No genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 61413, "total_output_tokens": 4171, "total_tokens": 65584, "total_latency_ms": 66779, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}